            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "text": "The authors define mixed-state partition functions by a supremum over pure-state decompositions, claim that this preserves faithfulness to the convex hull of stabilizer states, and define a channel partition function using its normalized Choi state. They explicitly leave monotonicity of the extended quantities for future work. This is an unverified author-claim candidate."
      }
    ],
    "conditions": [
      {
        "condition_id": "condition:mixed-channel-extension-0",
        "origin": "SOURCE_RECONSTRUCTED",
        "source_span_refs": [
